Ò"No one knew where she had come from. She was just a scrap of a girl clinging to a black cat with eerie yellow eyes. A lost child or an orphan, maybe. It was a miracle she had survived on Eden Mountain at all. Suddenly strange things began to happen in placid Ruger County, bizarre killings that the police couldn't solve. Horrifying accidents that the people couldn't comprehend. An insatiable beast was stalking their lovers' lanes, their swimming holes, and their children. No one noticed how quickly the little girl's pale cheeks turned pink with health. How her frail body filled out with sleek, lithe muscles and feline grace. And no one noticed that at night her innocent blue eyes turned an eerie, evil yellow ...""Ö
ÓImagine a young, intelligent woman who has immigrated to the United States in hopes of living the American dream. She has put herself through school and finally found her path in life. Success seems to be almost within her grasp.But Candelaria Enredame is a magnet for trouble. Her Santeria powers are strong, but very unpredictable. As a result, her life is a continual rollercoaster of excitement and danger, a fast-paced combination of comedy, mystery, and romance.She lands a great job as the accountant for a new luxury resort and casino, but the place is cursed. The new casino is being constructed on old tribal land and haunted by the ghost of a massacred Indian maiden. Legend has it that there is Spanish treasure buried somewhere in the hills that surround the place, the last remains of a violent confrontation with the Indians centuries ago.
Author's Biography
Lee Roberts is an accounting manager for a large international company with more than twenty years of experience in global business and finance. He is a licensed C.P.A. and holds a M.B.A. from the University of Tennessee as well as a B.S. degree in Information Technology. Lee is originally from the Southeastern U. S., but his wife is from the grand historical city of Cartagena, Colombia. Their life together is a bilingual mix of North and South American culture that combines the best of both worlds. Lee's writing draws on his years of business experience as well as the many interesting people that he meets along the way. His stories are based on the fascinating dynamics of life and celebrate the great mysteries of human diversity. Lee currently lives in North Carolina with his wife, three cats, and kids on the way. He has a web site at http: //www.loroberts.com"ø
õTom, a foundling, is discovered one evening by the benevolent Squire Allworthy and his sister Bridget and brought up as a son in their household; when his sexual escapades and general misbehavior lead them to banish him, he sets out in search of both his fortune and his true identity. Amorous, high-spirited, and filled with what Fielding called "the glorious lust of doing good," but with a tendency toward dissolution, Tom Jones is one of the first characters in English fiction whose human virtues and vices are realistically depicted. This edition is set from the text of the Wesleyan Edition of the Works of Henry Fielding."	
